# You design and build LEGO Technic models one step at a time, in a build language.
#
# For each step you write:
# ADD name partnumber color
# CONNECT part.point -> part.point LOCKED|TURNS|STIFF   (points: hole1.., axlehole1.., pin1.., axle1.., clip1..; LOCKED = cross in cross, turn together; TURNS = free; STIFF = friction pin)
# Optional: MESH a.teeth b.teeth / RATIO a b x/y / GROUP g (opens a side build) / END (closes it) / ATTACH g (joins a finished side build into the main model)
# WHY one plain sentence: what this step builds and what it is for.
# A point ending in ~ is an estimate; ? means not known.
#
# Rules: only use real points of each part; a round pin never goes in a cross hole; a shaft that must turn needs round holes; a worm needs stops on both sides; gears must sit at the right distance.
STEP 1
ADD beam-1 32524 black
WHY Starts the model with a long 7-hole beam that the differential assembly will build onto from both ends.

STEP 2
ADD conn-1 32184 yellow
ADD joint-1 32014 darkgray
CONNECT conn-1.hole1? -> beam-1.hole1?
CONNECT joint-1.hole1? -> conn-1.axlehole1?
WHY Mounts a yellow angle connector on the beam's first hole and stacks a dark gray 90-degree joint on top of it, leaving the joint's axle stub free for the housing.

STEP 3
ADD ring-1 18654 yellow
ADD joint-2 32014 darkgray
CONNECT ring-1.hole1? -> beam-1.hole7?
CONNECT joint-2.hole1? -> ring-1.hole1?
WHY Adds a bearing sleeve on the beam's last hole and a second 90-degree joint on top of it, starting the opposite arm of the differential.

STEP 4
ADD housing-1 60c01 black
CONNECT housing-1.stub1? -> joint-1.axlehole1?
WHY Drops the 24-tooth differential housing onto joint-1's free axle stub, seating the gear case at the beam's near end.

STEP 5
ADD ring-2 18654 yellow
ADD conn-2 32184 yellow
CONNECT ring-2.hole1? -> beam-1.hole2?
CONNECT conn-2.axlehole1? -> ring-2.hole1?
CONNECT conn-2.hole1? -> housing-1.stub2?
WHY Braces the housing against the beam with a second yellow connector and sleeve so the case can't twist as the gears inside turn.

STEP 6
ADD bevel-1 6589 tan
ADD axle-1 4519 yellow
ADD ring-3 18654 yellow
CONNECT bevel-1.axlehole1 -> axle-1.axle1 LOCKED
CONNECT axle-1.axle2 -> joint-2.hole1 TURNS
CONNECT ring-3.hole1 -> axle-1.axle3 TURNS
WHY Builds the right output half-shaft: a tan bevel gear locked onto a yellow axle that turns in joint-2's socket and meshes with the gears inside the housing, with a sleeve as an end bearing.

STEP 7
ADD bevel-2 6589 tan
ADD axle-2 4519 yellow
ADD ring-4 18654 yellow
CONNECT bevel-2.axlehole1 -> axle-2.axle1 LOCKED
CONNECT axle-2.axle2 -> housing-1.hub1? TURNS
CONNECT ring-4.hole1 -> axle-2.axle3 TURNS
WHY Builds the matching left half-shaft, passing its axle into the housing's bore so both output shafts mesh with the gears inside the differential case.

STEP 8
ADD tube-1 18654 darkgray
ADD gear-1 3648 darkgray
ADD gear-2 3648 darkgray
ADD bush-1 3713 red
ADD bush-2 3713 red
ADD bracket-1 32523 black
ADD conn-3 32184 yellow
ADD tube-2 18654 yellow
ADD tube-3 18654 yellow
ADD tube-4 18654 darkgray
CONNECT gear-1.axlehole1? -> housing-1.stub3?
CONNECT gear-2.axlehole1? -> housing-1.stub4?
CONNECT tube-1.hole1 -> housing-1.hub2? TURNS
CONNECT bush-1.axlehole1 -> axle-1.axle2 LOCKED
CONNECT bush-2.axlehole1 -> axle-2.axle2 LOCKED
CONNECT bracket-1.hole1? -> housing-1.stub5?
CONNECT conn-3.axlehole1? -> bracket-1.hole2?
CONNECT tube-2.hole1? -> bracket-1.hole3?
CONNECT tube-3.hole1? -> conn-3.hole1?
CONNECT tube-4.hole1? -> housing-1.hub2?
WHY Finishes the differential: two more 24-tooth gears and a sleeve mesh with the bevels inside the housing, a bush stops each half-shaft from sliding, and the last connector, beam, and sleeves close out the parts list as a mounting bracket on the housing.
